-      "conclusion": "The actual invocation SourceOrigin retains its complete original image/channel after token stamping, with full configuration and independently supplied ContextRegistry on command tokens. Positioned lowering body buffers cannot replace that whole-source owner. Source-restoration and nested-word transport preserve that owner. The analyser diagnostic build supplies its actual availability generation; a foreign command store declines rather than replacing it from a profile label. The descriptor revalidates original unchanged words and invokes the common guarded hosted metadata issuer. Known custom or missing cells block nominal schema selection, while unknown alternatives retain explicit authored-coordinate and applicability obligations. Getter metadata can produce only possible taint, and sink metadata can produce conditional warnings with the original source spans. Neither path supplies sanitiser certainty, storage effects, execution reachability, Native command selection, Normal completion, compiler admission or edit equivalence. Equality compares complete structural context and source/configuration independently of presentation. At an exact original sole-variable sink operand, private HostedSourceRead retains the guarded hosted metadata and actual positioned SsaSourceView. Only its independent read_reference receipt can select a cell and contents version; missing cell, version or taint keeps an unknown MAY value rather than consulting an SSA display-name clean default. Whole original word correspondence is mandatory. Native sink paths retain their separate physical read rules. Actual selected hosted setter source warnings use their independent genuine F5 source issuer and full Module ownership. Missing supplied input withholds the conditional warning.",
